---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const platforms = [
  'Google Workspace',
  'Microsoft 365',
  'Dropbox',
  'Box',
  'Amazon Web Services',
  'Azure',
  'Google Cloud',
  'Adobe Creative Cloud',
  'Slack',
  'Notion',
  'Airtable',
  'HubSpot',
  'Salesforce',
  'QuickBooks',
  'Xero',
];
---

<Base
  title="Systems | Griffith Creative"
  description="We help companies build the systems that suit how they actually work. Storage, software, and the workflows between them, reviewed and rebuilt around the team."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container-site hero-grid">
      <p class="eyebrow">Systems</p>
      <div class="hero-body">
        <h1 class="h1">Tools that fit how you work.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          We help companies build the systems that suit how they actually work: storage, software, and the workflows&nbsp;between&nbsp;them.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Book a call</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site two-col">
      <h2 class="h2">The review</h2>
      <p class="para">
        Most companies run on systems nobody chose. Tools were added one at a time, files went wherever there was room, and the way work moves between people was never designed. Over two weeks we sit with your team, learn how the work really happens, and write up what is helping, what is in the way, and what it&nbsp;all&nbsp;costs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site two-col">
      <h2 class="h2">The rebuild</h2>
      <p class="para">
        Then we build the version that fits. Archives go somewhere they can be found. Overlapping tools become one. The hand-offs people do by hand start happening on their own. Scoped from the review, priced in writing, and built around the way your&nbsp;team&nbsp;already&nbsp;works.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site">
      <h2 class="h2 mb-8">What we work with</h2>
      <!-- The full list is legible at desktop widths. On a phone it becomes a sentence,
           which reads faster than fifteen wrapped pills. -->
      <p class="para lg:hidden mb-8">
        Google Workspace and Microsoft 365, the storage and cloud platforms behind them, and the design, finance and sales tools most companies&nbsp;already&nbsp;run.
      </p>
      <ul class="hidden lg:flex flex-wrap gap-2.5 mb-8" aria-label="Platforms">
        {platforms.map((platform) => <li class="tag">{platform}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="para">If your company runs on it, we have most likely worked in it. If not, we learn it before we&nbsp;touch&nbsp;it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-close">
    <div class="container-site close">
      <div class="close-main">
        <h2 class="h2-close">Systems that work the way you do.</h2>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Book a call</a>
      </div>
      <div class="close-next">
        <a href="/process/" class="next-link">How we work</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
